{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Nevertheless a spring or a cistern, a gathering of water, shall be pure</b> — He says that the waters in a mikveh do not receive impurity by virtue of their attachment to the ground if the impurity falls into them. And he said, \"and one who touches their carcass shall become impure\" — its measure is: and waters that touch their carcass shall become impure, for the detached waters that touch their carcass become impure, since in a mikveh the waters do not touch their carcass, but rather their carcass falls into it. And he mentioned the waters in singular form, in the manner of \"water of impurity is not sprinkled upon him\" (Numbers 19:13). Alternatively, the verse says \"and all who touch their carcass shall become impure,\" and the intent is to include the waters and the liquids mentioned above (Leviticus 11:34). And as a general principle, this comes to teach about the waters that they receive impurity when detached but not when attached, for this was not mentioned until now. And in Torat Kohanim (parashah 9:6), Rabbi Yosi HaGelili says: \"and one who touches their carcass shall become impure\" — by contact they impart impurity, but not by carrying. And this too is possible, that it refers back to all the matters mentioned, and he says that the creeping things have only impurity of contact. And our Sages further have midrashim on this verse from the extra wording, all of them being halakhah leMoshe miSinai. And he mentioned the purity of the mikveh and the attached waters in the context of creeping things, and the same applies to carcasses, but he waited until he had finished mentioning all the species of things that impart impurity. Or it is because the way of creeping things is to die in a spring or a cistern. And I have already mentioned my opinion (Ramban on Leviticus 11:32)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:05.089953180Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}